nd the time for his installation having arrived, on terraces and houses, and doorways boys playing in bodies, conversed with each other concerning the installation of Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-6-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2006016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c66da9e1a05702d0e8194fd809a7ee9e7353748fd3a9728928223411ab2859c","compact":"819635fa1daf9c3e075cb866c352e40f1dac534844fbf61cc0889275be41eb87","nasal":"819635fa1daf9c3e075cb866c352e40f1dac534844fbf61cc0889275be41eb87"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-6-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":6,"verse":17,"english":"On the occasion of the investiture of Rāma, the goodly high ways were adorned with garlands, and scented with dhūpa incense, by the citizens.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-6-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2006017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"435b16290650f173a3b5896927bd0f51ac113fc979dfc2613a2e9c42a8c51282","compact":"1aab90ef7995bf37f611da87ad2e6a749779ccd2cb18c5c2653038f83db02ccb","nasal":"95f48ca1cc040663f97b87a6a1ccc07e9002e1a987e596ac46df744384ed1630"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-6-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":6,"verse":18,"english":"And fearing lest Rāma should come out over night (to behold the beautified capital), the inhabitants of the city, by way of ornamentation as with the view of beholding Rāma himself, had by the road side reared up lamp-stands in the form of (branched) trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-6-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2006018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d215467104d77a281bc2b